.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt UL 1
.Os FreeLinX
.Sh NAME
.Nm ul
.Nd do underlining
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm ul
.Op Fl t Ar terminal
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads its input and translates underlining and overstriking sequences
produced by programs such as
.Xr man 1
into terminal specific escape sequences, writing the result to
standard output.
.Pp
If no
.Ar file
is given, or if
.Ar file
is
.Ql - ,
standard input is read.
The terminal is selected with the
.Fl t
option, defaulting to the
.Ev TERM
environment variable.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr man 1 ,
.Xr terminfo 5 ,
.Xr tput 1
.Sh HISTORY
An
.Nm
command appeared in 4.2BSD.